            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0219" n="172" sameAs="frus:frus1981-88v13/pg172"/>

                <head>83. Memorandum From Acting Secretary of State Eagleburger to President Reagan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d83-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1982-04-08">April 8, 1982</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to the situation in the South Atlantic.]</p>
                <p>2. <hi rendition="#italic">Falklands:</hi>
                    Bill Middendorf succeeded in persuading
                    the OAS to adjourn until Monday<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d83-f2"/> without substantive debate on an OAS good offices resolution proposed chiefly by Colombia.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d83-f3"/> Meanwhile, I met separately with the French and
                    German Ambassadors to discuss the Falklands situation. Each Ambassador indicated
                    his nation’s solidarity with the UK, support for
                    the Secretary’s efforts to defuse the crisis, and concern about the implications
                    of a military clash.</p>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to the situation in the South Atlantic.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
